License: other
 Each icon is the logo of the application it stands for, shown only to name
 that application in the catalogue. The logos and their trademarks belong to
 their owners. remmina.png comes from Ubuntu's remmina package (GPL-2+).
 These come from the packages the App Center installs, under the licences
 their copyright files give: klickety.png (Ubuntu's klickety, GPL-2+),
 ktouch.svg (ktouch-data, GPL-2+), kolourpaint.svg (kolourpaint,
 BSD-2-clause), leocad.svg (leocad, GPL-2), tuxtype.svg (tuxtype, GPL-2),
 exelearning.png (eXeLearning's own .deb, AGPL-3+) and anydesk.svg
 (AnyDesk's own .deb; AnyDesk's trademark). spotify.png is the logo Flathub
 shows for com.spotify.Client, Spotify's trademark. The website apps show
 icons of the desktop's icon theme, not the websites' logos.

